      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Code Simplicity \u0026 Idiomaticity:** `GWRITE_FIELD` evaluates `GREG32(mname, rname)` three times. Since `GREG32` expands to `REG32(get_reg_addr(...))` and `get_reg_addr` performs a linear string search (`strcmp`), this will result in three linear lookups per field write.\n\nConsider using a `do { ... } while(0)` block to evaluate the register address exactly once, assuming this macro is only used as a statement:\n```c\n#define GWRITE_FIELD(mname, rname, fname, fval) \\\n\tdo { \\\n\t\tvolatile uint32_t *__reg \u003d (volatile uint32_t *)get_reg_addr(GNAME(mname, rname)); \\\n\t\t*__reg \u003d (*__reg \u0026 (~GFIELD_MASK(mname, rname, fname))) | \\\n\t\t\t (((fval) \u003c\u003c GFIELD_LSB(mname, rname, fname)) \u0026 GFIELD_MASK(mname, rname, fname)); \\\n\t} while (0)\n```\n*(If `GWRITE_FIELD` is required to yield a value as an expression, consider adding a static inline helper function instead).* [🔗](http://go/tj/58a79ec6-5c5e-41e5-aecf-3b4302fdbeff)",
